    "result": "Perfect! I've successfully implemented the `--threshold` feature for `frai eval`. Here's a summary of what was added:\n\n## Implementation Summary\n\n### Core Changes\n\n**1. frai-core/src/eval/index.js** - Threshold validation logic\n- Modified `generateReport()` to accept optional `thresholds` object\n- Validates each threshold by checking metric scores against minimums\n- Treats null scores as failed thresholds\n- Adds `passed` (boolean) and `thresholds` (array) fields to reports only when thresholds are provided\n- Backward compatible - reports without thresholds are unchanged\n\n**2. frai-core/src/eval/reporters.js** - Markdown output\n- Enhanced `toMarkdown()` to include a \"Thresholds\" section showing PASS/FAIL status for each threshold with min/score values\n\n**3. frai-core/src/eval/index.test.js** - Test coverage\n- Added 3 test cases covering passing thresholds, failing thresholds, and null score handling\n\n**4. frai-cli/src/index.ts** - CLI integration\n- Added `parseThresholds()` function with strict validation:\n  - Format validation: `metric=value`\n  - Metric ID validation (exact_match, toxicity, length_variance)\n  - Value range validation (0-1)\n  - Clear error messages listing valid metrics for unknowns\n  - Exits with code 2 for usage errors\n- Modified `runEvalCommand()` to parse thresholds and exit with code 1 on failure\n- Added `--threshold <metric>=<min>` option (repeatable) to eval command\n\n### Behavior\n- **Exit codes**: 0 (pass/no threshold), 1 (threshold fail), 2 (usage error)\n- **Reports**: Always written; JSON reports gain `passed` and `thresholds` fields; Markdown gets a \"Thresholds\" section\n- **Backward compatible**: Without `--threshold`, behavior is identical to before\n- **SDK support**: `generateReport()` accepts thresholds object and works with custom metrics\n\nAll changes are in the working directory and ready to be committed.",
